<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="error_prompt.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="error_prompt">
    <!-- debugmsg error report (debug_error_prompt). Opened LAST, so it stacks on top
         of whatever document the error interrupted — the whole point: the curses
         version painted underneath any open document and could only be dismissed
         blind. The model is filled once before the document loads and never changes;
         the keyboard (raw inp_mngr events, no input_context) owns space/i/c and
         scrolls #err-report from C++, while the mouse wheel scrolls it natively. -->
    <div class="panel err-panel">
        <div class="err-title" data-rml="title_rml"></div>
        <div id="err-report" class="err-report" data-rml="report_rml"></div>
        <div class="err-hints" data-rml="hints_rml"></div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
